REFERENCE FILE: tmp/reference_autumn.riv (1626 bytes, 133 objects, fileID=2274415)
OUR FILE:       docs/preview/fromjson_autumn.riv (1073 bytes, 97 objects, fileID=0)

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DIFF SUMMARY BY CATEGORY
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[BY DESIGN — not bugs]
1. PointsPath(16)+CubicPathVertex(35) vs Ellipse(4)
   Reference uses real leaf silhouettes built from cubic bezier paths.
   We use parametric Ellipses. Functionally equivalent for the renderer.

2. Forward parentId references in reference (SolidColor.parentId points to
   a Fill that appears later in the stream). Our file uses strict topological
   order (parent always appears before children). Both are valid per spec.

3. Leaf initial positions: reference starts leaves ABOVE artboard (Y<0)
   so they fall INTO view. Our file starts leaves within artboard (Y=20-260).

4. fileID=0 vs fileID=2274415. Our builder emits fileID=0 (no GUID). The
   reference was saved by the Rive Editor with a generated GUID. No rendering
   effect.

5. Extra LayoutComponentStyle (typeKey=420) in reference. Layout-only metadata
   from the Rive Editor, no visual effect.

6. Reference has 6 Fill objects (5 per leaf + 1 for the Artboard itself with
   SolidColor 0xFF282828 dark background). Our file uses a sky Rectangle shape
   for the background instead.

[POTENTIALLY SIGNIFICANT]
7. FillRule: reference emits key#40=2 (even-odd) on ALL Fills. Our file does
   not emit FillRule (defaults to 0, non-zero winding). For convex parametric
   shapes (Ellipse, Rectangle), this makes no visual difference — both rules
   produce identical fill for non-self-intersecting paths.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ROOT CAUSE HYPOTHESIS (after 8 tasks, still unconfirmed)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Static analysis shows the binary is structurally CORRECT:
  - parentIds: all verified correct via manual trace + rivdiff
  - animation targets: all KeyedObject.objectIds match leaf Shape art-rel indices
  - Fill/SolidColor chains: all parented correctly

The ONLY structural difference between autumn_leaves (broken) and working
ellipse demos (dots, easing, color_fade, ellipse_test) is:
  autumn_leaves has a FULL-ARTBOARD BACKGROUND RECTANGLE as its FIRST child
  before the leaf Ellipses.

Hypothesis: The Rive @rive-app/canvas v2 runtime renders artboard children
in REVERSE of stream order (first-added child = rendered LAST = on top).
This would cause sky (first child, art-rel 1) to render on TOP of all leaves
(art-rel 5, 9, 13, 17, 21), making them invisible.

Evidence FOR this hypothesis:
  - All broken shapes (leaves) come AFTER sky in the object stream
  - Sky (only visible shape) comes FIRST in the stream
  - All working demos have only ONE type of shape, so Z-order doesn't manifest
  - dots/easing have ellipses at non-overlapping positions — Z-order irrelevant

Evidence AGAINST:
  - Standard 2D scene graph renders first=bottom, last=top
  - Rive Editor's own reference file has all leaf Shapes first (before Fills),
    which would also be "on bottom" if order is normal, yet the reference works

NOTE: The reference's success doesn't help resolve this because it has NO
sky rectangle — all shapes in the reference are leaves, so Z-order doesn't matter.

